[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 457,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 370,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65713,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 419,
        "headingId": 370,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Myofibroblastoma of the lower genital tract is a benign neoplasm comparable to myofibroblastoma of breast, composed of myofibroblastic cells, bands of hyalinized collagen, and usually an adipocytic component.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:22:43"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 458,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 371,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65714,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 419,
        "headingId": 371,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>8825/0 Myofibroblastoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:22:43"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 459,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 372,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65715,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 419,
        "headingId": 372,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>EE6Y &amp; XH3NQ0 Other specified fibromatous disorders of skin and soft tissue &amp; Myofibroblastoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:22:43"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 460,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 373,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65716,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 419,
        "headingId": 373,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Acceptable:</em> mammary-type myofibroblastoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:22:43"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 461,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 374,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65717,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 419,
        "headingId": 374,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:22:43"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 462,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 375,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65718,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 419,
        "headingId": 375,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Approximately 50% of cases occur in the inguinal/groin area, including the vulva/vagina and perineum; however, there is a wide anatomical distribution {11474286; 26523539}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:22:43"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 463,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 376,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65719,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 419,
        "headingId": 376,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Tumours generally present as slow-growing, painless (or occasionally painful) masses or as incidental lesions {26523539}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:22:43"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 464,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 377,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65720,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 419,
        "headingId": 377,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Myofibroblastoma predominantly affects adults in the fifth or sixth decade of life, but the age range is wide (4&ndash;96&nbsp;years; median: 54&nbsp;years).</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:22:43"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 465,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 378,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65721,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 419,
        "headingId": 378,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:22:43"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 466,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 379,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65722,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 419,
        "headingId": 379,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Loss of 13q14, including <em>RB1</em>, is characteristic of myofibroblastomas, which are pathogenetically related to other benign mesenchymal lesions within the 13q/<em>RB1</em> family of tumours, including spindle cell&nbsp;/ pleomorphic lipoma and cellular angiofibroma {22575260; 26523539; 20852591; 27825811}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:22:43"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 473,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 386,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65723,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 419,
        "headingId": 386,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The size ranges from &lt;&nbsp;1&nbsp;cm to 22&nbsp;cm (median: 6.6&nbsp;cm). The tumours are generally well circumscribed, mobile, and rubbery to gelatinous. The cut surface may be whorled or nodular with fatty areas and variable coloration.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:22:43"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 467,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 380,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65724,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 419,
        "headingId": 380,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Tumours are unencapsulated, well circumscribed, and composed of spindle cells arranged in variably sized but typically short fascicles, with interspersed broad bands of hyalinized collagen or (less commonly) ropey collagen. The spindle cells have short stubby nuclei with finely dispersed chromatin, small or inconspicuous nucleoli, eosinophilic to amphophilic cytoplasm, indistinct cell borders, and sometimes elongated cytoplasmic processes. Scattered mast cells are often present. Tumours vary in cellularity from markedly cellular to paucicellular and hyalinized. There is usually an admixture of mature adipocytes, which can be minimal or occasionally the dominant component. Schwannoma-like palisading, focal epithelioid or round cell morphology, or degenerative-type nuclear atypia can occur {26523539}. Blood vessels are generally small and inconspicuous and are often hyalinized with a perivascular lymphocytic infiltrate.</p>\r\n<p>Myofibroblastoma typically shows diffuse coexpression of desmin and CD34 (each positive in 90% of cases). Rare cases are negative for one or both markers. Expression of SMA is present in one&nbsp;third of cases. About 90% of cases show loss of nuclear RB1 {22790852; 26523539}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:22:43"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 468,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 381,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65725,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 419,
        "headingId": 381,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:22:43"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 469,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 382,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65726,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 419,
        "headingId": 382,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>RB1 loss (by immunohistochemistry or FISH) is seen in the majority of cases.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:22:43"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 472,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 385,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65727,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 419,
        "headingId": 385,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> circumscribed tumour; haphazardly intersecting short fascicles of bland spindle cells; bands of hyalinized collagen; a variable adipocytic component.</p>\r\n<p><em>Desirable:</em> expression of CD34 and desmin; RB1 loss (by immunohistochemistry or FISH) in selected cases.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:22:43"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 470,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 383,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65728,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 419,
        "headingId": 383,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:22:43"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 471,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 384,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65729,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 419,
        "headingId": 384,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Myofibroblastomas are benign tumours; local recurrence is rare even if the margins are positive.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:22:43"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]